Fixtures for adapter/acp. CONSTRUCTED FROM ACP'S PUBLISHED EXAMPLES, NOT
RECORDED TRAFFIC: no real merchant, buyer, card or token. Every value comes
from the Agentic Commerce Protocol repository at commit
7fdd78df677a94dce04c770644b0fbbb1401272b, re-serialized as JSON with
two-space indentation and a final newline. The bytes of each file are the
fixture's "octets as delivered".

checkout-session.json
  examples/2026-04-17/examples.agentic_checkout.json
  member create_checkout_session_response
checkout-session-with-order.json
  examples/2026-04-17/examples.agentic_checkout.json
  member complete_checkout_session_response
delegate-payment-response.json
  examples/2026-04-17/examples.delegate_payment.json
  member delegate_payment_success_response
order-event.json
  spec/2026-04-17/openapi/openapi.agentic_checkout_webhook.yaml
  postOrderEvents requestBody example order_created (the body only).
  The order events in examples.agentic_checkout.json are not used: both
  fail JS-CHK $defs/Order (no id; a refunds member the schema removed).
order-event.http
  The same body octets as order-event.json, after a POST request line and
  header fields. Merchant-Signature is OAS-WH's own parameter example
  (t=1709123456,v1=e3b0...b855). It is not an HMAC of this body under any
  secret; the adapter never runs the HMAC, so its value is never checked.
mcp-checkout-session.json
  A JSON-RPC 2.0 response {"jsonrpc", "id": 2, "result"} constructed around
  examples.agentic_checkout.json member get_checkout_session_response, as
  docs/mcp-binding.md "Response Mapping" describes. The MCP examples in
  examples.mcp.agentic_checkout.json are not used: their results omit
  fulfillment_options, which JS-CHK requires.
trust-policy.json
  Pins acp.carried_digest to the SHA-256 of checkout-session.json.
leg-checkout-session.json
  CONSTRUCTED, not recorded: a minimal settlement-records leg (no envelope
  signature; the Capsule envelope is not this adapter's to verify) whose
  settlement.wrapped[] holds one entry of type acp.checkout-session (a type
  acp-v0 open point A-3 proposes; not registered) with content =
  checkout-session.json's octets, base64url without padding, and digest =
  their SHA-256. The settlement members other than wrapped are placeholders.
